  "response": "## Finding\n\n`crime_00070` (`duplicate_component_shape`) — the 9-line `<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">` footer (Cancel link → submit Button) is repeated verbatim across the 4 invoice form files.\n\n## Files that change\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:142-150`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:152-160`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:101-109`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:112-120`\n\nPlus a new file per project:\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n\n## Shared component\n\n**Name:** `InvoiceFormActions`\n\n**Public API**\n\n```ts\ntype InvoiceFormActionsProps = {\n  cancelHref: string;          // currently always \"/dashboard/invoices\" — kept a prop so the\n                               // component is reusable from other invoice flows\n  submitLabel: string;         // \"Create Invoice\" | \"Edit Invoice\" — only thing that varies today\n  submitDisabled?: boolean;    // optional; lets forms gate submission on validation state\n};\n```\n\n**Slots:** none. The two children (Cancel link, submit Button) are fixed in structure; only the label and href vary. If a future form needs an extra action (e.g. \"Save as draft\"), promote the right-hand side to a `children` slot then — premature now.\n\n**Shape**\n\n```tsx\nexport function InvoiceFormActions({ cancelHref, submitLabel, submitDisabled }: InvoiceFormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        Cancel\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\" aria-disabled={submitDisabled}>{submitLabel}</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nEach call site collapses to `<InvoiceFormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />` (or `\"Edit Invoice\"`).\n\n## Caveats\n\n- The `final-example` and `starter-example` directories appear to be separate apps (each has its own `app/lib/utils.ts`, `app/lib/data.ts`, `app/ui/...` — see findings 5–45), so a single shared component crossing both isn't appropriate. Extract once per app rather than hoisting to a cross-app package.\n- The button label is the only behavioral variation; if your design system already has a primary-action footer pattern, prefer reusing that over introducing `InvoiceFormActions` as a sibling.",
